  "description": "Human-friendly duration parsing and formatting for .NET: \"1h30m\", \"90s\", \"2 days 4 hours\", \"PT1H30M\", and \"1:30:00\" all parse to TimeSpan, and TimeSpan formats back in Go, verbose, colon, ISO-8601, or compact style. One permissive grammar unifies Go time.ParseDuration syntax (including its full test vectors as the oracle), word syntax with singular/plural units and \"and\"/comma tolerance, TimeSpan colon syntax, and ISO-8601 durations with loud rejection of calendar year/month components. Ships a TypeConverter so \"timeout\": \"30s\" in appsettings.json binds straight to TimeSpan through Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration, and a System.Text.Json converter for JSON payloads. Span-based allocation-free parsing, invariant culture everywhere, fail-loud errors with position info, fuzz-tested TryParse, zero external dependencies.",
